Willow Discord Bridge
=====================

This project contains substantial work adapted from Hush:

  Hush — Mute Discord while you dictate
  Copyright (c) 2026 Matthys Ducrocq
  https://github.com/MatthysDev/hush

Hush introduced the core design used here: observe the user's existing dictation
shortcut and control Discord self-mute through Discord's local RPC interface,
without injecting keyboard events. The gesture state machine, Discord RPC/OAuth
approach, and portions of the associated tests were adapted from that project.

The original MIT License and copyright notice are retained verbatim in LICENSE.
The upstream README is preserved in UPSTREAM_README.md for additional provenance.

This repository's Windows-specific adaptation includes a Rust/Tauri tray
lifecycle, a native Win32 low-level keyboard hook for Willow Voice shortcuts,
direct Discord named-pipe RPC and OAuth, Windows DPAPI credential protection,
a WebView2 settings interface, Windows packaging, and related tests.

